            <ArticleTitle>A bruital headache and double vision.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>147-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 44-year-old woman presented with a painful abducens nerve palsy in the left eye. Examination revealed a white, quiet eye and an orbital bruit without proptosis. Magnetic resonance imaging demonstrated abnormal ipsilateral dural-based enhancement. Angiography confirmed a posterior draining carotid-cavernous fistula. Symptoms resolved spontaneously in approximately 8 months. The classification and treatment options for carotid-cavernous fistula are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
